cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, the Lutar Invariant family, the Audit Closure Operator Λ₁₀, or the Ouroboros Thesis v10, please cite as below."
title: "Ouroboros Thesis v10 — EXHAUSTIVE-AUDIT: The Audit Closure Operator Λ₁₀ over the Lutar Invariant Family (v1 → v7 + Ω)"
abstract: >-
  v10 of the Ouroboros thesis chain introduces the Audit Closure Operator
  Lambda_10, a machine-verifiable meta-invariant over the v1..v7+Omega Lutar
  family established in v9. For each layer L_k, A_k = L_k * product over six
  artefact-presence indicators (CODE, CODEX, API, TEST, THESIS, SURFACE);
  Lambda_10 = sum_k A_k. Closure theorem: Lambda_10 / sum L_k = 1 iff every
  artefact is present for every layer. Strictly inert in the all-operational
  limit and quantifies operational drift exactly otherwise. Shipping artefacts:
  lutarV10Audit (TypeScript), POST /api/ouroboros/lutar/v10, codex node
  lutar_v10, an 8-test contract suite, A11oy /thesis row v10, and Sentra
  /thesis mirror. v10 introduces no new physical L-term; it formalises the
  v9 implementation contract.
